Context
  The plugin directory reported: "The security scan flagged v0.1.0 e29e9a3 for
  a reviewer ... Reason: Reports usage to an outside endpoint." Located by
  grepping for hard-coded http:// addresses: skills/guile-repl-server/SKILL.md
  named a fixed private IP twice, once in the requires network list and once in
  a rule instructing GET /ports/<port> then POST /claim with node, repo, pwd,
  kind and a mandate.

Considerations
  - pwd is the part that makes this a usage report rather than a port check: it
    sends the absolute path of whatever the agent is working on off-box.
  - The operator's global CLAUDE.md mandates this registration, so removing it
    from the skill does not change behaviour on these machines. The distinction
    is audience: a house rule applies to the operator's hosts; a skill applies
    to every installer, none of whom can reach that address.

Deviations
  - Version stays 0.1.1 rather than taking a second bump. Per RELEASING.md this
    is patch work: no skill was removed or renamed, no bin/*.sh argument or
    output contract changed, and nothing an installer could have scripted
    against is broken. The rule removed was an instruction to the agent, not an
    interface.
  - Generated benchmark transcripts under the *-workspace/ trees were not
    scrubbed. They are evidence of what the agent produced under the old
    instruction; rewriting them to match the new one would be falsifying a
    record this repo's whole argument depends on. If the scanner reads them and
    flags again, that is the honest answer to give the reviewer.
